{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>As a freewill offering you may make it.</b> Even though its blemishes are numerous and visible, and one might suppose that it is unfit even for bedek ha-bayit (temple maintenance), Scripture states that for nedavat bedek ha-bayit (a freewill offering for temple maintenance) it is fit, as transmitted in the tradition — since the altar has no share in it, and no sanctity rests upon it except the sanctity of its monetary value, so that it is sold and passes into profane use."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:19.152826372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}